+        // A shot that will be lip-synced sends no scene prose. Its still IS
+        // the scene, and the prose is what walks a second person into frame:
+        // it says the speaker is looking at someone "just off-frame" and then
+        // forbids that someone, which a video model reads as an invitation.
+        //
+        // Ordinary b-roll keeps its prose untouched. Most of these scenes have
+        // no person in them at all — flour, hands, a street — so a clause about
+        // holding a facial expression would be noise at best.
+        prompt: params.lipSynced?.[i] === true
+          ? characterScenePrompt({ visual, motion, lipSynced: true })
+          : `${visual}. ${motion}`,
